  "bio_summary": "Sunil Kumar is an Indian professional kabaddi player, born on May 12, 1997, in Haryana. He plays as a defender, primarily in the right cover position, and currently captains U Mumba in the Pro Kabaddi League. Kumar has achieved significant international success, including gold medals at the Asian Games (2022), Asian Championship (2023), and South Asian Games (2019) representing India. He is also recognized as the most successful captain in Pro Kabaddi League history, having led the Jaipur Pink Panthers to a championship title in 2022.",
